 "applies_to": "Yaskawa P7B drive/bypass packages (P7 drive CIMR-P7U inside a bypass enclosure, option V native Modbus) using the drive's RS-422/485 terminals, per technical manual TM.P7B.01 Appendix D.",
 "summary": "The P7B is a P7 fan/pump drive packaged with a bypass contactor panel and HAND/OFF/AUTO switch. Modbus RTU is served by the drive itself (option V, native protocol) using the same hex register layout as the P7, except that 0001H bits 0/1 are run/stop and direction. This map covers the Appendix D reference and monitor data and the Enter commands.",
